# The human-assist extension IS tracked here, but only in its SANITIZED form,
# produced reproducibly by scripts/sanitize-human-assist-extension.mjs.
#
# These two entries make it impossible to re-introduce the upstream artifacts
# the sanitizer deliberately strips:
#
#  - secrets.txt is a 2048-byte encrypted blob the upstream service worker uses
#    to derive the EXTENSION AUTHOR'S default wit.ai speech keys. Those are a
#    third party's credentials; Homatch configures a backend it owns instead
#    (HUMAN_ASSIST_SPEECH_API_KEY -> chrome.storage.local, per job).
#  - _metadata/ holds Chrome Web Store integrity artifacts that apply only to
#    store-installed packages. Chromium deletes the directory when loading an
#    unpacked extension, so tracking it would guarantee a dirty working tree.
human-assist/secrets.txt
human-assist/_metadata/
